60,3,1,talk,May,,"Option A sounds like a recipe for disaster! ""Maintained by whoever uses them"" is just a fancy way of saying the same person will end up cleaning everyone's crumbs. We need a system, not a free-for-all!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Misaki,,"Option A would only exacerbate the current issues. If we encourage more food preparation in a room that already leaks noise and mess into the office, our workstations will become even more compromised. It is not a viable solution.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Servas,,"Option B offers a sanctuary for the soul, yet I fear it may be a lonely victory. If we silence the room, do we not simply push our conversations back to the desks where they were once awkward?","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Sakura,,"Option C is the answer to the mystery! We're paying 68,000 yen for outside rooms because we don't have a place for meetings! If we pick C, we save all that money and get a cool screen!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Kenji,,"@Sakura, you're totally right about the money! But @Servas is right too—we can't just be lonely. Option C is great because it gives us a private place to finally have those tough talks without everyone listening!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Sakura"",""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,May,,"@Sakura, @Kenji, you're both so focused on the money and the talks! But look at Option C—it has a ""shared calendar governing its use."" Finally! A way to stop the first-come, first-served chaos and make things actually fair.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Sakura"",""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Misaki,,"@May, a calendar provides order, but the primary benefit of Option C is the containment of activity. By designating it as a meeting space, we can better manage the noise and prevent the office from becoming a dining area.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Servas,,"It is heartening to see such alignment. Option C provides a structure that respects both our time and our boundaries. By bringing our meetings home, we cease the weary journey to the main road and reclaim our hours.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Sakura,,"@Servas, exactly! No more long walks to the main road! Plus, the fit-out for Option C is 141,000 yen, but we're already spending so much on those hourly rooms. It's like buying a toy that saves us money! I vote for Option C!","{""words"":43,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"I'm with Sakura! Option C is the only one that solves everything. We save money, stop the crumbs at the desks, and most importantly, we finally have a place to actually talk and be a team! I vote for Option C!","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,May,,"@Sakura, @Kenji, you've almost sold me on the ""saving money"" part, but I'm mostly just thrilled about that calendar! No more guessing games or cleaning up after mystery guests. I'm in. I vote for Option C!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Sakura"",""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Misaki,,"@May, the calendar is a useful detail, but the reduction of disruption is the real priority. Option C is the only choice that addresses the noise and mess issues while providing a necessary function. I vote for Option C.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Servas,,"When we align our needs with a sustainable structure, we find a path that honors everyone's effort. Option C removes the burden of travel and the chaos of unplanned use. I vote for Option C.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Sakura,,"Yay! Everyone is agreeing! It's like we all found the missing puzzle piece together! No more wasting money on that other room, and we get a fancy screen! I'm so happy! I vote for Option C!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Kenji,,I'm so glad we're all on the same page! This is going to be awesome. We'll finally have a place to be honest with each other and grow as a team. I vote for Option C!,"{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,May,,"It's a total landslide! I'm just glad we're finally getting some order around here. No more ""first-come, first-served"" madness for me! Let's make this meeting space the most organized spot in the office. I vote for Option C!","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Misaki,,The consensus is clear. Option C is the only responsible choice that resolves the spillover of noise and mess into our workspace while fulfilling a practical need. I vote for Option C.,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Servas,,"It is a beautiful thing when a group finds harmony. By choosing a path that values both our time and our peace, we ensure that no one is left to carry an unfair burden. I vote for Option C.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Sakura,,I'm so happy we all agree! We solved the mystery and saved the ice cream money! Now we can have our own special spot for everything! I vote for Option C!,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Kenji,,"I'm so happy we did this! We're not just saving money, we're building a place where we can actually be friends and support each other. I'm voting for Option C!","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
